course: dictionary
lesson: 9652
title: Subjective and objective
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Subjective means based on someone's own feelings, tastes or opinions. It is not something everyone can check, because different people can see it differently.
explain: «Art is partly a matter of taste, which means different people like different things.» Whether a painting is beautiful depends on the person looking at it, so that is subjective.
explain: The opposite is objective: based on facts that anyone can check or measure. The length of a pencil is objective, because you can measure it with a ruler and get the same answer as anyone else.
explain: In grammar, the subjective case is a different idea. It is the form of a pronoun used as the subject of a sentence: I, he, she, we and they, but not me, him, her, us or them.
fact: Subjective means based on someone's own feelings, tastes or opinions.
fact: Objective means based on facts that anyone can check or measure.
fact: «Which song is best is subjective.»
fact: In science, measuring with instruments reduces subjective judgement.
fact: The subjective case is the form of a pronoun used as the subject of a sentence: I, he, she, we, they.
exercise: «Which song is best is subjective.» What does subjective mean here? | *Based on a person's own taste or opinion | Based on facts that anyone can check | Written by a famous band | Easy to sing along to
exercise: Which of these is an objective fact? | *The box is 10 centimetres long | Blue is the nicest colour | The film was boring | This pizza is the tastiest food in the world
exercise: Which word is a pronoun in the subjective case? | Me | Us | *They | Him
test: Which statement is subjective? | *Dark chocolate is the tastiest sweet | The door is two metres tall | The table has four legs | The book has 200 pages
test: Which sentence uses the subjective case correctly? | *We went home | Me and him went home | Them went home | Us went home
exam: Why is a review of a film usually subjective? | It uses only numbers | It gives the exact running time, which anyone can check | *It gives the writer's own feelings and tastes about the film | It is printed in a book
